## Slash Commands

This project ships with Claude Code slash commands in `.claude/commands/`. Use them to run
common workflows without writing long prompts:

| Command    | What it does                                      |
|------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| `/dev`     | Start frontend + backend dev servers              |
| `/build`   | Production build for both services                |
| `/test`    | Run the full test suite                           |
| `/commit`  | Stage and commit changes with a conventional message |
| `/review`  | Review current diff for quality and security      |{% if backend_framework == "django" %}
| `/migrate` | Create and apply Django database migrations       |{% endif %}

Invoke with arguments for extra context, e.g. `/review frontend/src/App.tsx`.

